  "term": "AIS",
  "definition": "AIS stands for Automatic Identification System, a source of vessel trajectory data used to study and predict ship movement. In this context, AIS data can be simplified to reduce repeated route information while preserving movement continuity, which can improve learning tasks such as trajectory prediction and anomaly detection.",
